comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:12:25.217Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status corpus3042/3042 including closed items has no occurrence of either advisory or predecessor GHSA-82fw-gwwq-j7x9. Live request-specific searches and open/in_progress inventories found no exact advisory owner; semantic-only search results are not duplicate evidence. Reuse the security epic; keep the broader Vitest5 migration separately open."
  "2026-10-21T21:17:06.131Z","harness:codex","Boundary and compatibility evidence: both public plugin regressions fail against4.1.11 and pass against4.1.12. The generated-source test executes only a harmless synthetic sentinel in a disposable Node child and also verifies exact URL preservation, quotes/backslashes/newlines in export names and asynchronous binding updates. The redirect test exercises the real registration handler and Vite allowlist without reading any files, rejects slash/backslash and nested escapes, and preserves an allowed redirect. This tests the normalization-to-allowlist boundary portably; native Windows CI remains required before merge. No tracked application config registers these public handlers, so no CLI/SDK exploit is claimed."
  "2026-10-21T21:17:07.307Z","harness:codex","Fresh patched evidence at21:13UTC: both feeds complete over all568 locked versions with zero positives; the previous hosted569-version receipt remains the positive before-control. Frozen installation, build and all typecheck targets pass. Existing retry/reporter/CodSpeed runtime cohort passes7/7, new handler regressions pass2/2, and the dedicated benchmark invocation succeeds. Paired4.1.12 packages satisfy pnpm default one-day age without exclusions; Vitest5 and CodSpeed6 migration remains separate."
  "2026-10-21T21:20:56.971Z","harness:codex",Independent candidate review found no concrete surviving bypass or regression. It traced all three shared serialization sites and redirect normalization before allowlist admission and the unchanged checked-path read. Additional read-only controls covered nine redirect representations and five export-name classes. Linux boundary execution passed; native Windows acceptance and whole-project coverage remain required hosted gates before merge.
  "2026-10-21T21:59:32.085Z","harness:codex","Pre-merge verification correction: final required Windows jobs pass, but their focused native cohort does not select the new installed-mocker boundary file; Ubuntu coverage alone does not satisfy the recorded native Windows acceptance criterion. Reopen this canonical lineage before editing the existing Windows cohort and its workflow contract. Preserve earlier before/after controls and closure history; no duplicate issue or weakened check is needed."
  "2026-10-21T22:02:54.218Z","harness:codex","Windows selection repair: the existing partition contract fails before the native advisory step is added (missing step), then passes with the suite selected only in the native cohort. The complete local workflow+handler cohort passes24/24, and linked dependency/retry/reporter plus workflow commands pass31/31. Build/typecheck/lint/workflow permissions pass. Preserve all three Windows partitions, the12-minute cohort budget and strict aggregate outcomes. Prior head f304eb2 passed26 required checks and100% coverage, but did not run these advisory probes on Windows; the new reviewed head must prove that native step before merge."
